                                                "sense_id": "29b82cf9-7822-3688-bb55-879c20575e98",
                                                "text": "1734, James Jurin, George Berkeley (Bishop of Cloyne), Geometry no friend to infidelity\nNow, we know that the several compound Ideas of a rectangled, an oblique, and an acuteangled Triangle are different and inconsistent one with another. No two of them can be put together so as jointly to exist or be conceived in the mind."
